# Backport of Omarchy b83d3df0840504299d3099ebf391eb8110527edd
# "Qualify shell palette references for Qt 6.12 (#14553)" (David Heinemeier
# Hansson, 2026-10-08; github.com/basecamp/omarchy, after v4.0.4).
#
# Why: Qt 6.12 adds a Color type to QtQuick, which shadows the shell's
# qs.Commons Color singleton, so every unqualified palette reference
# (Color.lock.text, ...) is undefined and the shell loses its theme colours.
# Arch Linux ARM ships Qt 6.12, and Omarchy's edge channel (the only one with
# aarch64 builds) still has 4.0.4 without the fix.
#
# The same mechanical change as upstream, on 4.0.4's files: import
# qs.Commons as Commons (after "import qs.Commons", or after "import QtQuick"
# in the Commons singletons) and write Commons.Color for every palette
# reference. Of the 285 changed lines, 284 are identical to lines of the
# upstream commit; the other is 4.0.4's own (LockView.qml's fingerprint icon
# colour). Upstream's other files (the elsewhen panel, PasswordlessSudo,
# BackgroundIntro) don't exist in 4.0.4. Drop this patch once the edge
# channel ships an Omarchy that contains b83d3df.
